  "generated_text": "1. **Identify the direction vectors of the lines:**\n   - The direction vector of the first line is $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -k \\\\ k \\end{pmatrix}$.\n   - The direction vector of the second line is $\\begin{pmatrix} 1/2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}$.\n\n2. **Set up the condition for coplanarity:**\n   - Two lines are coplanar if and only if their direction vectors are linearly dependent. This means there exist constants $a$ and $b$ (not both zero) such that:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -k \\\\ k \\end{pmatrix} = a \\begin{pmatrix} 1/2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n     \\]\n   - This gives us the system of equations:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{cases}\n     1 = a/2 \\\\\n     -k = a \\\\\n     k = -a\n     \\end{cases}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Solve the system of equations:**\n   - From the first equation, we find $a = 2$.\n  ",
